course: dictionary
lesson: 1152
title: Brightly in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brightly is an adverb. It tells you how something shines, looks, or is done. Its meaning changes a little with the words around it. «Saturn's rings shine brightly, as fresh snow does.» Shine is the clue: brightly means shining with a lot of light.
explain: Look at the word it sits next to. «Brightly coloured liquid capsules have been mistaken for sweets by small children.» Here brightly is about colour: the capsules have strong, bright colours that catch the eye, so small children think they are sweets.
explain: Brightly can also describe a mood. If someone «smiled brightly», they looked cheerful and happy. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Brightly is an adverb: it describes how something shines, looks, or happens.
fact: Brightly can mean with a lot of light, in strong colours, or in a cheerful way.
fact: «Brightly coloured» means in strong, bright colours, like the lemmings in «Norwegian lemmings are bold and brightly coloured».
fact: Fluorescent colours «glow brightly in daylight», but reflective material is what shines back in headlights at night.
fact: Safety tip: wear brightly coloured or reflective clothes so drivers can see you.
exercise: «Saturn's rings are made of water ice, and the ice makes them shine brightly, as fresh snow does.» What does shine brightly mean here? | Shine in a sad, slow way | Make no sound at all | Shine only in the dark, very quietly | *Shine with a lot of light, strongly
exercise: «Brightly coloured liquid capsules have been mistaken for sweets by small children.» What does brightly coloured mean? | Very cold to touch | *In strong, bright colours | Hidden under a cloth | Made of ice
exercise: Nadia says, «She smiled brightly when she won the race.» What does smiled brightly mean? | Smiled very slowly and quietly | *Smiled in a cheerful, happy way | Smiled with a lot of light | Smiled and then ran away
test: «A screen is made of millions of tiny dots called pixels, and all three glowing brightly together look white.» Find and copy the word that tells how the pixels glow. | white | millions | tiny | *brightly
test: Why do safety teachers say, «Wear brightly coloured or reflective clothes»? | So your clothes last longer | So you stay warm | So you can run faster | *So drivers can see you
exam: Which phrase means cheerfully? | Burn brightly | Shine brightly | Brightly coloured | *Smile brightly
